  "worked_solution": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe predictor equation of the modified Euler method with step size $\u0394x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394{y}_{p}={y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initially predicted new $y$-value is then given by ${y}_{p}=y+\u0394{y}_{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{\u2032}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =2x+y \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\u0394{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $\u0394{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394{y}_{p} & ={y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\u0394{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+\u0394{y}_{p} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\u0394{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
